@20 = ~Temple of Selûne~
@21 = ~Barracks~
@22 = ~Armorer~
@23 = ~Fletcher~
@24 = ~Balduran's Seatower~
@25 = ~Halfslinger~
@26 = ~A list of the day's guard duties. Boring.~
@27 = ~A larger-than-life statue of Balduran. The statue more closely resembles an eight-foot-tall ogre, about to topple at any moment.~
@28 = ~It simply says 'Balduran'. It doesn't look like any portrait of Balduran that you've ever seen.~
@29 = ~Piles of stones ready for the trebuchets on the roof.~
@30 = ~The trapdoor is locked.~
@31 = ~Temple of Ilmater~
@32 = ~The book cover reads 'The Book Of Future Memories'. Below the title, it says 'I am all colors and I am none'. You can't open the book no matter what you do.~
@33 = ~Tannery~
@34 = ~Catacombs~
@35 = ~Seatower Inn~
@36 = ~Dragon Tower~
@37 = ~Golden Dragon Ale~
@38 = ~Master Usher's Finest Clothes~
@39 = ~Treasury~
@40 = ~Chionthar Tower~
@41 = ~Traitor's Tower~
@42 = ~Chain Tower~
@43 = ~Dradeel's Tower~
@44 = ~South Harbor Tower~
@45 = ~Harbor Tower~
@46 = ~East Tower~
@47 = ~Slave Trader's Meeting Point~
@48 = ~Master Shizell's Magic Items~
@49 = ~This is the famous and *locked* alestore.~
@50 = ~Seatower Well~
@51 = ~Seatower Beacon~
@52 = ~While investigating the book, you find a blackened lens hidden in its spine.~
@53 = ~It is not a voice you can hear, and yet the words are clear: 'This book opens only for <PRO_HESHE> who received the scroll.'~
@54 = ~This is a tomb of the Shattershield Patriar family.~
@55 = ~This is the tomb of the Guthmere Patriar family.~
@56 = ~Prison Entrance~
@57 = ~You see a heavy door down there. This seems to be the entrance to the Seatower prison.~
@58 = ~A statue of a humanoid figure. It looks ancient, the stone weathered to an extent it is not clear what it is supposed to be.~
@59 = ~This portal door is inactive and leads nowhere.~
@60 = ~A display of sea creatures, motionless as if they were frozen. Oddly, it doesn't feel particularly cold.~
@61 = ~A display of smaller sharks.~
@62 = ~You see a huge octopus.~
@63 = ~There are several turtles here.~
@64 = ~You can't make out what is in here, the glass is murky.~
@65 = ~You see several eels or eel-like fish.~
@66 = ~This display is empty.~
@67 = ~There are swordfish here.~
@68 = ~Chapel~
@69 = ~This door is magically sealed. Someone scratched an arrow pointing to the left on it.~
@70 = ~A big, deep hole in the ground. It goes deeper than you can see, and definitely deeper than you want to fall, too.~
@71 = ~The wall is paved with skulls of all shapes and sizes, but most of them are humanoid. They look ancient, probably remnants of the deity that was worshipped here. There are bones on the floor that look rather fresh. You suspect that they were left here by the sahuagin.~
@72 = ~There is a huge *something* in this display. You can't make out its whole outline, and it is clear that only part of the creature is visible. You are glad you won't encounter it underwater, and that it's dead, or at least somehow frozen in time.~
@73 = ~This ship looks more like a skiff, and you can see the damage to its hull. The pirates have already started repairs, but it will be quite a while before she can set sail again.~
@74 = ~This seems to have been the main entrance to the Old Temple. You see many winged figures. Whatever deity was worshipped here, if their element was air and flight, that would explain why their church had no problem building a temple on such a remote island.~
@75 = ~A barrel with apples.~
@76 = ~Bandit's Hidden Stash~
@77 = ~Smuggler Meeting Place~

