//******************
//Items
//******************
@496 = ~Seatower Proclamation~
@497 = ~Citizens of Baldur's Gate!

Let it be known that, by edict of the Grand Dukes, the famous Seatower of Balduran is henceforth open to the public! Donate at Selûne's temple, seek shelter in Ilmater's monastery, and enjoy the famous Golden Dragon Ale in Roryn's tavern. But be warned: there are rumors of hidden danger beneath the surface, and the waters are unusually calm this year.

Duke Eltan, Hammer 1368 DR.~
@498 = ~Ring of Improved Invisibility~
@499 = ~Even a lord or a lady has moments when they simply want to disappear and not be seen by anyone, be it to avoid increased public attention or to escape an assassination attempt. The wearer of such a ring has certainly heard the words "I don't know where they went, they were just here a moment ago" many a time as they slipped away unnoticed.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Cast Improved Invisibility on the wearer once per day~

@500 = ~Storeroom key~
@501 = ~This is the key you found on the cook in Balduran's Seatower. It opens the sheds in the kitchen's storeroom.~
@502 = ~Goose feathers~
@503 = ~A bag of goose feathers given to you by the cook's apprentice and destined to be turned into arrow fletchings by the Seatower fletcher.~
@504 = ~Tankard for Halfslinger~
@505 = ~A tankard of Golden Dragon Ale brewed by the cook in Balduran's Seatower. You don't particularly want to remember what it cost you.~
@506 = ~False Arla's Dragonsbane~
@507 = ~A notably poor copy of the original and famous Arla's Dragonsbane sling. After all you went through to get this, it really wasn't worth the effort, as the copy is only marginally better than an ordinary sling.


STATISTICS:

THAC0:  +1 bonus
Damage:  +1 (missile damage)
Weight: 0
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Sling
Type:  1-handed
Requires: 3 Strength~
@508 = ~Tower Prison Pass~
@509 = ~This pass will grant you access to the Seatower's Prison, located in the cellar of the tower. The entrance is down the stairs in the main tower.~
@510 = ~Almiran's Scroll~
@511 = ~This scroll is supposed to open a hidden door to some ruins in the Wood of Sharp Teeth.~
@512 = ~Alguine's Key~
@513 = ~Alguine's key opens the locked door in the Halls of Future Memories.~
@514 = ~The Key to the Catacombs~
@515 = ~This key opens the hidden door in the catacombs under Balduran's Seatower.~
@516 = ~The Key to the Chionthar Tower~
@517 = ~The key to the mausoleum in the Chionthar Tower. The Seatower catacombs lie below the tower.~
@518 = ~The Ogre's Bone Dagger~
@519 = ~The blade of this dagger is made of a bone cut from some long-dead and forgotten monster. The edge is still as sharp as the day it was carved—and cursed.~
@520 = ~The Woman's Human Skull~
@521 = ~The blackened and scorched skull has survived the fire which should have destroyed it.~
@522 = ~The Sorcerer's Candle~
@523 = ~This candle contains a single Wish spell. In taking it, you denied the Sorcerer his last request.~
@524 = ~The Warrior's Talon~
@525 = ~The creature that once owned this desiccated talon did not live on this plane.~
@526 = ~The Poisoned Man's Antidote~
@527 = ~A thick red fluid stirs menacingly in the bottle. In taking it, you denied the Poisoned Man his life.~
@528 = ~The note just says: "Helm and Cloak, three days at the latest."~
@529 = ~The Book Of Planes~
@530 = ~You found this old book buried in the far corner of Alguine's library. You can try to read the book, but the more you read, the less sense it makes. Much of the book seems to be... missing... and the rest of it seems to be written by someone not much older than a child. Worse yet, each time you open the book, the pages have changed.~
@531 = ~Lars' Drawing~
@532  = ~This is the drawing given to you by Lars, the orphan boy. The picture bears a slight resemblance to what could be a dragon. You have absolutely no idea what you would use this for, but if you just dump it, a child will be very sad and a kitten will die somewhere, probably.~
@533  = ~Rabbit Cage~
@534  = ~This is the cage Inn Master Roryn gave you to collect all the rabbits from the third floor of Balduran's Seatower Inn.~
@535  = ~Betsy the Rat~
@536  = ~This is the rat you caught on the second floor of the Seatower Inn. It is unusually fat and has a tiny pink ribbon on its tail, with "Betsy" carefully written on it.
The rat looks at you, but shows no intent to bite you.~
@537  = ~This is the carcass of the rat you killed on the second floor of the Seatower Inn. You can still see a tiny pink ribbon on its tail, with "Betsy" carefully written on it.~
@538  = ~Slave Trader's Pamphlet~
@539  = ~This is the slave traders' contact information you received from the smugglers. It is an advertisement for "wild animal excursions" organized by "Leonhard the Fierce", who can be met on the third floor of the Seatower inn. There is a handwritten note on the back that says "ask for the special creatures tour".~
@540  = ~Sealed Box~
@541  = ~The box is light, and nothing moves inside when shaken.~
@542  = ~Slave Trader's Notes~
@543  = ~These are the notes you found on the body of "Leonhard the Fierce", the slave trader contact. It contains a schedule of a variety of innocent-sounding excursions.
There is one entry with a date in the future called "Special Creatures Pursuit".~
@544  = ~[#73906 (BGII)]Ring of Anti-Venom~
@545  = ~[#73913 (BGII)]This ring is an unadorned silver band. However, its plain appearance belies the powerful magic within. A Ring of Anti-Venom is eagerly sought after by royalty, influential political figures and other potential assassination targets.

STATISTICS:

Wearer is immune to all poison.~
@546  = ~Enshelled Black Pearl~
@547  = ~Pearls consist of layers of aragonite agonizingly formed around a bit of grit or other irritant inside oysters and other mollusks. The resulting pearl has a rich, deep luster. Most of the pearls in the realms are white, however there are rarer varieties such as rainbow and black. This pearl is black, a highly valued variant for their unique magical properties, particularly by diviners.

This pearl is fresh from its shell and gleams with seawater.~
@548  = ~Tailor's Key~
@549  = ~This key opens the locked door inside the tailor's shop in the Docks District.~
@550  = ~Mimic Powder~
@551  = ~This is what Master Shizell called "mimic powder". It is in fact a liquid, not a powder, and it is effective in unmasking doppelgangers, not mimics.
The flask is not completely stoppered and small wisps of fumes can be seen coming out of it. The flask needs to be used quickly before its effectiveness fades. When brought in close proximity to a doppelganger, the fumes–inoffensive on their own–combine with the odors of the Seatower and its environs into a scent that drives doppelgangers into a rage, shifting into their natural forms and attacking.~
@552  = ~Herb Liqueur~
@553  = ~This is a very dusty bottle of herbal liqueur from some faraway distillery.
This looks like a bottle that is best kept safe until you can give it to the right connoisseur.~
@554  = ~Empty Mimic Powder~
@555  = ~There is no more content inside the flask. The potion is no longer effective against doppelgangers.~
@556  = ~Treasury Note~
@557  = ~This treasury note entitles the bearer to a sum of 3,000 gold, to be collected in the Seatower Treasury.~
@558  = ~This treasury note entitles the bearer to a sum of 5,000 gold, to be collected in the Seatower Treasury.~
@559  = ~This treasury note entitles the bearer to a sum of 20,000 gold, to be collected in the Seatower Treasury.~
@560  = ~Plum Liqueur~
@561  = ~This is a very exquisite-looking bottle of Calimshan Plum Liqueur.
This looks like a bottle that is best kept safe until you can give it to the right connoisseur.~
@562  = ~Bitter Liqueur~
@563  = ~This is a very exquisite-looking bottle of Amnian Bitter Liqueur.
This looks like a bottle that is best kept safe until you can give it to the right connoisseur.~
@564  = ~This treasury note entitles the bearer to a sum of 500 gold, to be collected in the Seatower Treasury.~
@565  = ~Empty Barrel~
@566  = ~This is an empty barrel.~
@567  = ~Barrel full of Water~
@568  = ~This is a barrel full of water.~
@569  = ~Fire Resistant Barrel~
@570  = ~This barrel was coated on the inside with a fire-resistant layer by the Seatower fletcher. It should hold a fire elemental for at least a day.~
@571  = ~Barrel with Fire Elemental~
@572  = ~You trapped the fire elemental from the kitchen's storeroom inside this barrel.
The barrel feels slightly hot and you hear a low crackling like from a fire from time to time.~
@573 = ~<CHARNAME>'s Golden Dragon Ale~
@574 = ~A tankard of Golden Dragon Ale brewed by the cook in Balduran's Seatower. Getting it was a bit bothersome, but it was poured for you with best intentions in mind.

STATISTICS:

Dexterity:  -2 penalty
Special:  Prevents fear
Duration:  15 turns~
@575  = ~Sea Troll's Sebaceous Gland~
@576 = ~The sebaceous gland you gained from a sea troll. It's constantly oozing a gelatinous substance that is said to protect metal against water exceptionally well.~
@577 = ~Focus Lens~
@578 = ~This is a lens used for focusing light beams.~
@579 = ~Black Lens~
@580 = ~This crystal is round like a lens but completely black and opaque.~
@581 = ~Troll Almanac~
@582 = ~[BG:EE #32739]Trolls are horrid carnivores that are most well known for being hard to kill. All trolls regenerate, and most can only be killed through the use of fire.~
@583 = ~Flask with Water~
@584 = ~This is a flask of drinkable water.~
@585 = ~Fire Elemental Almanac~
@586 = ~Fire elementals emerge from the Elemental Plane of Fire, utilizing scorching flames as portals to traverse dimensions. Lacking flames to sustain their vigor, their power wanes swiftly. Hence, they relentlessly seek fiery conflagrations, which serve as conduits to their native realm.~
@589 = ~The Book Of Future Memories~
@590 = ~Lord Dlusker's Journal~
@591 = ~This seems to be Lord Dlusker's personal notes. It tells about the family's financial struggles and the lord's increasingly frantic attempts to overcome them.
The last page reads:
"I now have the means to ask Aldabert II personally about the hidden treasure! To think that the priests wanted 1,000 gold pieces for one Speak with Dead, while I got my hands on a Temporary Resurrection for just 200!
I'm looking forward to seeing Margot's face when I can tell her about a treasure chest in our home! I won't tell her just yet, she'll be too scared about me performing such a ritual.
The monks assured us that the mausoleum is safe despite some increased undead activity in the catacombs. I didn't plan on going there, anyway, so I do not see a problem. Plus, I have my grandfather's magical necklace that will protect me from any misfired magic.
The monks' warning will be the perfect excuse to make Margot wait outside so she doesn't have to worry, though (and, hand on heart, will also stop her from interfering)."~
@592 = ~Scroll with Myrkul's Symbol~
@593 = ~This is a scroll covered with several symbols.
Although you are not able to read it, the scroll seems ready to be used by whoever is holding it.~
@594 = ~Dead Rat~
@595 = ~This is a dead rat. It looks surprisingly intact and was placed so you *had* to find it.~
@596 = ~Ring of Life Force~
@597 = ~This ring does not look much, but it is clearly enchanted with magic. It has a fine engraving stating "For A. in Love". You found this ring on one of the corpses under the tailor shop.~
@598 = ~This ring does not look like much, but has a fine engraving reading "For A. in Love". You found this on one of the corpses under the tailor's shop.

STATISTICS:
  +4 to maximum HP total while equipped
~
@599 = ~Ring of Acid Immunity~
@600 = ~This ring was artistically crafted of green metal and adorned with a valuable gemstone. You found this on one of the corpses under the tailor shop.~
@601 = ~This ring was artistically crafted of green metal and adorned with a valuable gemstone. You found this on one of the corpses under the tailor shop.

STATISTICS:
  Acid Resistance set to 100%
~
@602 = ~Ring of Weapon Skill~
@603 = ~As unusual as it may seem that a ring has been enchanted with a property to improve weapon skills, it fits in perfectly with the environment of noble ladies and lords who do not want to walk around in heavy armor and yet have a good reason to improve their ability to defend themselves—possibly even without any attackers being aware.

STATISTICS:

THACO:  +1 bonus
~
@604 = ~<CHARNAME>'s Ring of Gratitude~
@605 = ~This ring looks like a simple gold ring, but it is clearly enchanted with strong magic. It has an engraving which says "For <CHARNAME>, in gratitude." You received this as a belated token of appreciation from several thankful Patriar Families of the city of Baldur's Gate for your help against the doppelganger invasion.~
@606 = ~This ring looks like a simple gold ring, but it is clearly enchanted with strong magic. It has an engraving which says "For <CHARNAME>, in gratitude." You received this as a belated token of appreciation from several thankful Patriar Families of the city of Baldur's Gate for your help against the doppelganger invasion.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
 Raises wielder's charisma to 18
 Wearer regenerates 1 hit point every 30 seconds
~
@607 = ~This ring looks like a simple gold ring, but it is clearly enchanted with strong magic. It has an engraving which says "For <CHARNAME>, in gratitude." You received this as a belated token of appreciation from several thankful Patriar Families of the city of Baldur's Gate for your help against the doppelganger invasion.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
 Charisma:  +1 bonus
 Wearer regenerates 1 hit point every 30 seconds
~
@608 = ~Letter from Ivonne~
@609 = ~Letter from Balduin~
@610 = ~This is a love letter from someone called Ivonne to someone called Balduin. It smells of roses.~
@611 = ~This is a love letter from Balduin to Ivonne. It is signed with two intertwined hearts.~
@612 = ~This is another love letter from Ivonne to Balduin. She thanks him effusively for the nice drawing.~
@613 = ~Dear unknown reader,

We noticed that someone was reading our hidden correspondence. We moved our secret place elsewhere.

Nevertheless, you have our sincere thanks for not disturbing our communication. Take this as our token of appreciation.

Balduin and Ivonne~
@614 = ~Tooth of Iakhovas~
@615 = ~This relic is a tooth from Iakhovas, former lover of Umberlee. It was brought back by Balduran from his sea travels. Rumor has it that he came into possession of it when his ship was attacked by sahuagin.
He donated it to the Temple of Umberlee to gain the goddess's favor for further ventures and the newly fortified city of Baldur's Gate.
The tooth is sacred to the temple.~
@616  = ~Headband of Charisma~
@617  = ~This jewel-studded headband would already fetch plenty of attention on its own, but it bears a subtle enchantment that makes viewers see the bearer in a very positive light, regarding <PRO_HIMHER> as a great leader or trustworthy authority.

STATISTICS:

Charisma: set to 18~
@618  = ~Silver Dart of Selûne~
@619  = ~This small weapon has been blessed by Selûne, the  Moonmaiden, and as such, it has special powers against lycanthropes and other creatures only harmed by silver weapons, which are affected by the moon's pure silver light.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +2 bonus (+4 bonus vs. Lycanthropes)
Damage: 1D3+2 (+4 vs. Lycanthropes)
Damage type:  missile (piercing)
Special:  Returns to users hand once thrown
Weight: 0
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: Dart
Type:  1-handed
Not Usable By:
 Cleric
 Mage~
@620  = ~Silver Sphere Ioun Stone~
@621  = ~This silvery sphere has a powerful abjuration that protects the user from backstabs.

STATISTICS:
   Immune to backstab while equipped~
@622  = ~Longbow of Speed +2~
@623  = ~This enchanted longbow can launch deadly volleys of arrows. There is no known name or history; it seems to be a relatively recently made item that hasn't had the time to gather any real fame yet.

STATISTICS:

THAC0:  +3 bonus
Damage:  +2
Special:  1 extra attack per round
Weight: 3
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Longbow
Type:  2-handed
Requires: 6 Strength
Not Usable By:
 Druid
 Cleric
 Mage
 Thief~
@624  = ~Paladin's Plate +2~
@625  = ~This blessed suit of armor was created by the clergy of Lathander for the sole purpose of combating the constant threat of undead as well as fiendish monsters to Faerûn. It has had a great number of owners over the ages, most of whom lived short but exciting and action-filled lives.

Armor Class: 1
Special: +2 bonus vs. demonic and undead
Weight: 25
Requires: 12 Strength
Only usable by: Good-aligned characters
Not Usable By:
 Bard
 Druid
 Mage
 Thief~
@626  = ~Ring of Illusions~
@627  = ~This ring and about a handful others similar to it were some three hundred years ago by a gnome thief/illusionist whose identity has been lost to history. It can cast a number of illusion spells on the wearer on demand. Although anyone can use it, it's a favorite of thieves and wizards who seek to befuddle and mislead their enemies.

STATISTICS:

Special Abilities:
  Blur once per day
  Invisibility once per day
  Mirror Image once per day
Requires: 14 Intelligence~
@628 = ~Dry Powder of Myconid Spores~
@629 = ~This is a cluster of myconid spores. The powder is completely dry, which allows the spores to persist for a long time.~
@630 = ~Hermit's Notes~
@631 = ~This is the notebook of the hermit in the library of the Old Temple Island. It is empty, with a lot of pages already missing.~
@632 = ~Boulder~
@633 = ~This is a fairly heavy boulder.~
@634 = ~Piece of Cheese~
@635 = ~This is a piece of cheese. It is a bit too ripe for your taste.~
@636 = ~Silver Fork~
@637 = ~Silver Fork of Balduran~
@638 = ~This is a silver fork, and it is... magical?~
@639 = ~The legends do not often speak of Balduran's Silver Fork, but that does not mean that it could not have been just as valuable to him as his Butter Knife. There is a small engraving at the shaft which fits the name, and it is of solid silver.
Someone enchanted it so it can be worn as a magic headgear. You are almost certain that this was not Balduran's doing, but you'll never know.

STATISTICS:

Armor Class Bonus:  None
Special:
  Protects Against Critical Hits
  Grants wearer infravision up to 120 ft
Weight: 0~
@640 = ~Tattered Amulet~
@641 = ~Tattered Greenstone Amulet~
@642 = ~This is a tattered Greenstone Amulet. When activated, the greenstone protects the wearer from all forms of mind attacks, including psionics. (note: it does not confer COMPLETE immunity to psionics)
It is still powerful, but it was holding only three charges when you received it.

STATISTICS:

Special Abilities:
This amulet confers the wearer protection against all charm, confusion, fear, domination, ESP, detect alignment, hold, stun, psionics, sleep and feeblemind. However the protection effect uses one charge each time it is used and will only last for 1 turn.~
@643 = ~Blood of Mighty Land Creature~
@644 = ~A vial of blood that imitates to come from a powerful land creature. The Old Hermit made it out of rat's blood, dry spore powder, and "quite some magic".
Applied to the portal built by the sahuagin in the "Arena" room, it should reverse the magic of a powerful sea creature used to create the portal and hopefully destroy the entire portal so that it cannot be used again.~
@645 = ~Gnawed Upon Note~
@646 = ~These are handwritten notes from the Old Hermit in the Old Temple library. The note is missing parts, visibly gnawed upon by small teeth.
This one is about the chapel on the first floor of the Old Temple halls. "I investigated it thoroughly—even jumped on the altar some until the priest told me to stop—but I couldn't find the mechanism that would open the passage to—"
The rest of the text is gone.~
@647 = ~These are handwritten notes from the Old Hermit in the Old Temple library. The note is missing parts, visibly gnawed upon by small teeth.
This one gives details about the Old Temple Island. You can make out that it is located in the Moonshae Seas, and that the Old Temple has lost its purpose to a point where it is no longer clear who was worshipped here. The details about which deities it could have been are no more readable due to the damage.~
@648 = ~Umber Hulk Hide~
@649 = ~This umber hulk hide consists of chitin plates and tough skin of a dark brown hue. Even off of the umber hulk's body, it looks thick and impenetrable.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 25~
@650 = ~Pink Waistcloth~
@651 = ~This is a very comforting waistcloth out of pink silk. The words "Girdle of Doom" are embroidered with an unsteady hand.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1~
@652 = ~Adventurer's Note~
@653 = ~Tuck,
since you insisted on it, I'll put it in writing that we'll divide the treasures we find neatly by 3. Maybe we can also ask the Umberlee bitches for an additional reward, if that tooth is so precious to them.
We just need to find the stupid thing, I'm sure your sneaking skills will make that a piece of cake.
Roger~
@654 = ~Craftsman's Hammer~
@655 = ~This is a craftsman's hammer, ideal for doing all kinds of carpentry work.

STATISTICS:

Damage:  1D4
Damage type:  crushing
Weight: 6
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: War Hammer
Type:  1-handed
Requires: 9 Strength
Not Usable By:
 Druid
 Mage
 Thief~
@656 = ~Handwritten Note~
@657 = ~These are handwritten notes from the Old Hermit in the Old Temple library.
"Since the deity worshipped here is probably long gone, just like their followers, it can't be the god itself that Umberlee despises so. My theory is that, despite the time that has passed, she still feels offended by the preserved sea creatures in the aisle windows. Killing them for such a display—the display itself—must go against everything the Bitch Queen holds sacred."
On the side, there is a scribbled note in the same handwriting: "One thing is clear: I probably shouldn't leave this place on a ship if I value my life. Unless I stock up on Water Breathing."~
@658 = ~These are handwritten notes from the Old Hermit in the Old Temple library.
"I found Balduran's Boots today. With the fork, this makes two items from the legendary pirate captain and founder of Baldur's Gate that were scattered on this island, but no other traces. How can this be?
My take on this is the following:
Balduran was a great seafarer who did not shy away from the stormiest seas. He also had his share of battles with sea creatures, and lost several ships to them or just the storms. Finding traces of him here does not necessarily mean that he was here himself; the items could have been washed ashore or carried here by the sea devils.
If he *was* here and inspected the temple ruins, it would explain why he was lost to the sea, though. Probably annoyed Umberlee one too many times, despite his efforts to soothe her by being on good terms with her church."~
@659 = ~These are handwritten notes from the Old Hermit in the Old Temple library.
"The sahuagin have taken up residence downstairs. I know that this place was frequented by them, but now they are staying here and they obviously have plans with this place. Since I assume that angering Umberlee is not their primary goal, I should sneak behind those guards and have a look at what they are doing in there.
Considering they need to submerge in seawater at least every few hours, it must be an official mission ordered by one of their kings. Considering they do this above the water, and their general aggressiveness toward the coasts and any land dwellers on them, it doesn't bode well."~
@660 = ~These are handwritten notes from the Old Hermit in the Old Temple library.
"I found where the other castaways are hiding today. They sealed themselves off with hidden doors. They are resourceful, I have to give them that.
The riddle to open the door is simple, but a good measure against the sahuagin, who either do not speak Common or loathe magic, and even more so against less intelligent monsters.
Still, I won't write the solution down, just in case. It's trivial enough, anyway. And a smart way of making use of all the displays of sea creatures, so to speak."
From the looks of it, the following remark was added later:
"And I have to admit, I am *so glad* they no longer hang out in the library. It got a bit crowded in here."~

@661 = ~Boots of Balduran~
/* #34011 #67469 sod */
@662 = ~These boots were supposedly worn by Balduran, the founder of Baldur's Gate. They were magically enhanced to protect against both Grease and cold feet, and seem worthy of the famous sailor he was known as.
There is a rumor that a mage friend of Balduran's added the Zone of Sweet Air spell after they spent weeks crammed together on a ship in stormy seas, but there is no record of this, so it could be a malicious rumor spread by whoever owned the used boots after our hero.

STATISTICS:

Special Abilities (once per day):
 Zone of Sweet Air
Equipped Abilities:
 Cold resistance:  +15%
 Immunity to Grease
Weight:  4~
@663 = ~The Key to the Hidden Door~
@664 = ~This key opens the hidden door on the lower inner level of the Old Temple Island ruins.~
@665 = ~Shell Horn~
@666 = ~This is horn made out of a seashell. It has a hole at the tip and has been carved a little into shape so it fits nicely into a humanoid hand.~
@667 = ~Ritual Note~
@668 = ~This is an old ritual note. You can hardly make out the words due to the state of decay:
"...however, if the soul were split, it would be hindered to advance to the afterlife. Not only would it stay...
...in a gaseous, nonmaterial form. Due to their restricted perception, the fragments will...
...need to prevent the fragments from meeting, otherwise the process will be reversed and the fragments will merge again, making the soul whole again, enabling them to..."~
@669 = ~Dagger +3~
@670 = ~[EE Description: #71036 BGII:EE]The typical dagger has a pointed, usually double-edged blade, as opposed to a knife, which has a single edge and is a bit shorter. This particular dagger is magical, having special bonuses to its speed, accuracy, and damage. Also, since it is magical, it is capable of striking opponents that are immune to normal weapons, such as vampires, elementals, and mummies.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d4+3 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Dagger
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 3 Strength

Weight: 0~
@671 = ~Candle~
@672 = ~A candle, as old as the ancient temple ruins, but still usable.~
@673 = ~Suth Timber~
@674 = ~This is the wood of a suth tree, known for its ability not to splinter even under heavy blows.~
@675 = ~Mother, I found a group of promising adventurers who took the bait and went through the portal. We should await their arrival and prepare, because it looks like they might not hand the Sacred Tooth back without causing trouble.~
@676 = ~Sister Muryial, how could you orchestrate such an unprofessional intrigue? Not only do the sahuagin attacks come at a time when the political situation is already destabilized and of *no* use to us. They have taken Iakhovas' Tooth, a sacred relic of our temple, to the Old Temple of the One We Shall Not Name!
Get the relic back, and quickly. I don't mind breaking some pact with the sahuagin, but I dread the moment when our goddess becomes aware that a sacred relic is being kept in such a blasphemous place.
And to make matters worse, Jalantha is becoming suspicious about the whereabouts of the Sacred Tooth. I can't put her off for much longer.~
@677 = ~The Key to the Prison Cells~
@678 = ~This key opens the prison cells in the Balduran's Seatower dungeon. It was given to you so you can speak to Tower Guard Shuck. It also seems to open the other cell doors, but the guards will see to it that those are not left unlocked for long.
You should hold on to this key if you want to talk to other prisoners later.~
@679 = ~Melly's Necklace~
@680 = ~This is a light gold necklace with a gemstone as a pendant. The engraving reads "Melly".~
@681 = ~Slythe,
Your terms are acceptable. The reason why I will only send you after three of the four Dukes is experience I've had with Eltan's defenses. After the fiasco of my last assassination attempt I turned to something more devious and subtle to get him out of the picture.
Be ready, I will let you know when the time to strike has come.

Sarevok~
@682 = ~Diary Page of Sarevok~
@683 = ~[The entry needs to start with a letter or it looks stupid in BGT]On the 16th of Marpenoth, 1366:
I should really start carrying my journal with me at all times. I want to record how things have developed, I want people to know later how I came to power. I'll write it here for now. Hopefully I'll find the time to transfer it to my real journal.
The attack on Eltan was a disaster and a brilliant maneuver in one. Eltan is not dead—my plans to start taking control of the Flaming Fist will have to wait a little longer. I underestimated his defense and how prepared he is for assassination attempts. He is targeted far too often. Next time I go against him I have to make sure it's more subtle, and I need to get rid of that forsaken second-in-command, first.
I also underestimated just how big a wave an attack on the commander of the Flaming Fist would cause. There is little to nothing that the public gets to see, but behind the curtains, it is dangerous to go against Eltan like this. I will keep it in mind.
Nonetheless, the whole thing went brilliantly. The 'evidence' I planted for safety and to cover my own tracks worked perfectly. That idiot Malastair, fifth cousin of Duke Eltan and contender for a leadership role at the Iron Throne, is now sitting in a cell in Seatower Prison, and will never see the light of day again! Making him a scapegoat was a brilliant plan. There seems to be a noticeable amount of rivalry and mistrust in Eltan's wider family, even more than I could have hoped for. He saw the fake correspondence and immediately suspected Malastair of trying to increase his influence in the Flaming Fist. It almost makes me laugh that this idiot is now in jail for what *I* want to accomplish. Anyway, my competitor is gone! Not only has he cleared the way for me to become one of the next leaders of the Iron Throne, but Rieltar now believes he can't trust anyone outside our family with his succession. No one but me!
This could not have gone better. I'll deal with Eltan later, I'll figure out a way to get behind his defenses—inside his trusted circle. I now have all the resources.~
@684 = ~Note from Prisoner~
@685 = ~This is the handwritten note from the imprisoned bandit. It seems to be written in some sort of code. You can't make anything of it.~
@686 = ~Big Box~
@687 = ~This is the crate the smuggler Edgar gave you. This should lure out the Night Masks who target the rival Black Lotus smuggling operation.~
@688 = ~Calimshan Fragrance~
@689 = ~This is a very fine, slightly dry fragrance for men that is highly sought-after in Calimshan.
It is usually very expensive. Well, if you don't buy it from smugglers, of course.~
@690 = ~Official Amnian Collaboration Pass~
@691 = ~You received this "Official Collaboration Pass" from Sergeant Telmov of the Nashkel Guard. It states that you are an official informant regarding smuggling activities around Nashkel.
You have the gut feeling that he might have second thoughts about giving this to you. If you do not start delivering intelligence, this pass will probably not work forever, or the sergeant could try to take it away again.~
@692 = ~Heavy Barrel~
@693 = ~This is an unusually heavy barrel. It is closed, but there are several smaller holes in the hull, as if the contents should be well ventilated.~
@694 = ~Confirmation about Smuggler Bust~
@695 = ~This is a written confirmation for your help in exposing smuggling activities in Baldur's Gate.~
@696 = ~Small Valuable Box~
@697 = ~This is the box Holger gave to you to hand to Bruce, a Flaming Fist in the palace.
When you shake it, you can hear the clink of coins. You have the impression that the box itself is quite valuable, too.~
@698 = ~Old Coin~
@699 = ~This is an old coin, its origin unknown to you. It seems to have been in the well for a very long time.~



//******************
// Journal entries
//******************

// Titles (more titles in between)
@700 = ~The Fletcher's Feathers~
@701 = ~Halfslinger's Ale~
@702 = ~The Tanner's Troubles~
